    "title": "SASEA Electricity Demand Data for 2013-2025",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17175212",
    "publication_date": "2025-09-22",
    "description": "<p>This dataset provides harmonised electricity demand records for twelve South and Southeast Asian (SASEA) countries:<strong> </strong>Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Malaysia, Myanmar, Nepal, Oman, Philippines, Singapore, Sri Lanka, Taiwan, and Thailand. The data cover the period 2013&ndash;2025, with availability varying by country.</p>\n<p>Raw demand data were collected from national utilities, regulators, and international agencies using online portals, automated retrieval scripts, and direct file downloads. All records were standardised to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Units: megawatt-hours (MWh)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Time format: ISO 8601 (daily or higher resolution)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Country codes: ISO 3166-1</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Processing steps included completeness checks, outlier detection, and adjustments for calendar and time-zone differences. Metadata and processing scripts are provided alongside the dataset to ensure reproducibility and transparency.</p>",
